---
import PhotoPlaceholder from '../PhotoPlaceholder.astro';
import SectionHead from '../SectionHead.astro';
---

<section data-vision-section class="band-cream section">
  <SectionHead num="7 / 14 — Place" heading="Beyond the living room." />

  <div class="container-page">
    <PhotoPlaceholder
      description="A neighborhood plaza in the Valley — a Sunday market, kids and adults using public space together. Not the Strip. A version of Henderson Town Square or downtown's Symphony Park, on a regular weekend."
    />
  </div>

  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="vision-prose">
      <p>
        We want tree-lined bike paths, bus stops with shade, and buildings that invite you to stay
        on the street instead of rushing through it. Parks within walking distance of every
        neighborhood — not one big regional park forty minutes away. Plazas wide enough for a Sunday
        market, libraries open evenings and weekends, community centers that look like front porches
        instead of DMV offices. Festivals that close streets rather than parking lots. And sidewalks
        you can actually use in July.
      </p>
      <p>
        The won Valley has all of this distributed across its town centers, not centralized in one
        place. Public space becomes the third place — neither home nor work — where Las&nbsp;Vegans
        actually run into each other. That is what city life is supposed to feel like. It's also
        what the social-science research keeps finding: loneliness runs lower where people have
        somewhere to be that isn't their living room or their office. Vegas can have it. The desert
        never stopped us; we just never built for it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
